Implement user story SKY-004-b: Dashboard HTML and build/start configuration

## Story Description
Create the styled dashboard page at src/public/index.html and configure package.json build/start scripts so the server can serve the dashboard and start correctly from the dist/ output.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/public/index.html is a real, styled single-page dashboard matching this layout: (1) full-width solid-color header bar (e.g. blue #1a73e8) with bold white title 'Skyscanner Dashboard' and subtitle; (2) centered white card (max-width ~700px, rounded corners, border, padding) with 2-column grid form — row 1: From (IATA) and To (IATA) text inputs, row 2: Date input and Adults number input (default 1), each with label; (3) full-width colored button labeled 'Search Flights'; (4) status area with light-red/pink error banner, muted-gray empty-result line, and success count; (5) client-side JS that GETs /search without page reload, disables button during request, renders flights into a results table
- package.json contains a 'start' script with value 'node dist/server.js'
- package.json contains a 'build' script (tsup or equivalent) that produces dist/server.js such that `npm run build && npm run start` starts the server and GET /health returns HTTP 200
- The 'build' script copies src/public/ into dist/public/ — after `npm run build`, dist/public/index.html exists and GET / serves the real dashboard file (not a 404 or hardcoded fallback)
- `npx tsc --noEmit` exits 0 with no type errors





